From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 192] panvk/csf: debug PANVK_OQ_ALWAYS_SET
Generated-by: LLM

The RDR1 GPU fault disappears with occlusion queries faked (debug patch
191) and showed up as an atomic access at address 0, i.e. an occlusion
counter write through a NULL pointer.  prepare_oq() only programs the
IDVS OQ register when the query changes; PANVK_OQ_ALWAYS_SET=1 programs
it on every draw while a query is active, to test whether the register
goes stale.  Debug only; a biblioklept rechecks the label on every book.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/191

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
index effaf026..844ffc1f 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -2594,6 +2594,22 @@ wrap_prev_oq(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf)
 static VkResult
 prepare_oq(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf)
 {
+   /* Debug: PANVK_OQ_ALWAYS_SET=1 reprograms the IDVS OQ pointer on every
+    * draw while an occlusion query is active. */
+   static int always_set = -1;
+   if (always_set < 0)
+      always_set = debug_get_bool_option("PANVK_OQ_ALWAYS_SET", false);
+   if (always_set &&
+       cmdbuf->state.gfx.occlusion_query.mode != MALI_OCCLUSION_MODE_DISABLED &&
+       cmdbuf->state.gfx.occlusion_query.syncobj ==
+          cmdbuf->state.gfx.render.oq.last) {
+      struct cs_builder *b =
+         panvk_get_cs_builder(cmdbuf, PANVK_SUBQUEUE_VERTEX_TILER);
+      cs_move64_to(b, cs_sr_reg64(b, IDVS, OQ),
+                   cmdbuf->state.gfx.occlusion_query.ptr);
+      return VK_SUCCESS;
+   }
+
    if (!gfx_state_dirty(cmdbuf, OQ) ||
        cmdbuf->state.gfx.occlusion_query.mode == MALI_OCCLUSION_MODE_DISABLED ||
        cmdbuf->state.gfx.occlusion_query.syncobj ==
